<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Get Connected on Splunk Observability Cloud Workshops</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/ninja-workshops/ai/3-splunk-agent-observability/1-get-connected/</link><description>Recent content in Get Connected on Splunk Observability Cloud Workshops</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/ninja-workshops/ai/3-splunk-agent-observability/1-get-connected/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Connect to EC2 Instance</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/ninja-workshops/ai/3-splunk-agent-observability/1-get-connected/1-connect-to-instance/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/ninja-workshops/ai/3-splunk-agent-observability/1-get-connected/1-connect-to-instance/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="create-a-ciscocom-account"&gt;
 &lt;span class="heading-text"&gt;Create a Cisco.com Account&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;a class="heading-anchor" href="#create-a-ciscocom-account" aria-label="Permalink" aria-hidden="true"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&amp;rsquo;ll need a Cisco.com account to complete this workshop. If you don&amp;rsquo;t already have an account,
navigate to &lt;a href="https://id.cisco.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;https://id.cisco.com/&lt;svg class="link-ext" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="M7 17 17 7"/&gt;&lt;path d="M9 7h8v8"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
 and complete the form to create your account:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure class="figure"&gt;
 &lt;div class="figure__inner"&gt;
 &lt;img src="../../images/CiscoRegistration.png" alt="Cisco Registration" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check your inbox for an email from cisco.com. If you don&amp;rsquo;t see the email, please check your spam folder.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Click on the link in the email to verify your email address.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sign In to Splunk Agent Observability</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/ninja-workshops/ai/3-splunk-agent-observability/1-get-connected/2-sign-in-to-splunk-agent-observability/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/ninja-workshops/ai/3-splunk-agent-observability/1-get-connected/2-sign-in-to-splunk-agent-observability/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="sign-in-to-splunk-agent-observability"&gt;
 &lt;span class="heading-text"&gt;Sign In to Splunk Agent Observability&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;a class="heading-anchor" href="#sign-in-to-splunk-agent-observability" aria-label="Permalink" aria-hidden="true"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To access Splunk Agent Observability, navigate to
&lt;a href="https://console.multitenant.sao.splunkcloud.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;https://console.multitenant.sao.splunkcloud.com`&lt;svg class="link-ext" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="M7 17 17 7"/&gt;&lt;path d="M9 7h8v8"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
 using your browser.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The credentials are stored as environment variables on your EC2 instance:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code-block"&gt;
 &lt;div class="code-block__header"&gt;
 &lt;span class="code-block__file"&gt;&lt;span class="code-block__lang"&gt;bash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;button class="code-block__copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy code to clipboard"&gt;Copy&lt;/button&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;$SPLUNK_AO_USER&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;$SPLUNK_AO_PASSWORD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Use these credentials to sign in to Splunk Agent Observability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After signing in, ensure that the &lt;code&gt;workshop&lt;/code&gt; org is selected. Then, you should see a screen
similar to the following example:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>